WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.318 --> 00:00:03.644
- Mr. Williams, you
reportedly came in last night

00:00:03.644 --> 00:00:04.482
'cause your--

00:00:04.482 --> 00:00:05.397
- My watch was stolen.

00:00:05.397 --> 00:00:07.122
- Your watch was stolen while on you.

00:00:07.122 --> 00:00:07.955
So you were mugged?

00:00:07.955 --> 00:00:08.788
- Yes.

00:00:08.788 --> 00:00:10.426
- Can you tell us, take us
through again what happened?

00:00:10.426 --> 00:00:12.088
- Yeah, basically I
was just on my way home

00:00:12.088 --> 00:00:13.730
from work last night.

00:00:13.730 --> 00:00:15.110
And I was waiting for the train.

00:00:15.110 --> 00:00:16.618
And this guy came up.

00:00:16.618 --> 00:00:18.732
I think he had a weapon,
I think he had a gun,

00:00:18.732 --> 00:00:21.232
and he just, he took my watch.

00:00:22.622 --> 00:00:25.425
- And I just, I need to--
- [Lady] Yeah, yeah.

00:00:25.425 --> 00:00:29.455
- When you put a watch on
like that, a flashy watch,

00:00:29.455 --> 00:00:31.767
who are you really wearing it for?

00:00:31.767 --> 00:00:33.933
(saxophone music)

00:00:33.933 --> 00:00:38.100
(logo whooshes)
(hinge squeaks)

00:00:40.331 --> 00:00:42.073
Look, I hate to say it but

00:00:42.073 --> 00:00:43.922
you just need to be more self-aware

00:00:43.922 --> 00:00:45.522
that when you wear a watch out like that,

00:00:45.522 --> 00:00:47.048
you're really just taunting people.

00:00:47.048 --> 00:00:48.439
- It's in our human nature

00:00:48.439 --> 00:00:50.271
to want to grab after wealth.

00:00:50.271 --> 00:00:53.087
And so a man strutting
around with expensive things,

00:00:53.087 --> 00:00:54.254
it's taunting.

00:00:55.872 --> 00:00:58.631
Men just can't dress nice
when the sun goes down.

00:00:58.631 --> 00:01:01.696
- Men generally shouldn't
wear a major brand label

00:01:01.696 --> 00:01:02.928
after dusk, really.

00:01:02.928 --> 00:01:04.354
I have two sons of my own at home.

00:01:04.354 --> 00:01:08.208
And I would never let them
out of the house after 7pm

00:01:08.208 --> 00:01:09.334
in anything other than sweatpants.

00:01:09.334 --> 00:01:10.167
- Yeah.

00:01:10.167 --> 00:01:11.998
You need to dress down.

00:01:11.998 --> 00:01:13.496
- Mr. Williams, were you drinking

00:01:13.496 --> 00:01:14.605
the night that this happened?

00:01:14.605 --> 00:01:15.782
- No, I just got off work.

00:01:15.782 --> 00:01:16.899
- Do you like to drink?

00:01:16.899 --> 00:01:18.077
Couple after work?

00:01:18.077 --> 00:01:19.577
Couple on weekend?

00:01:20.486 --> 00:01:22.827
- Did you try to disguise it?

00:01:22.827 --> 00:01:26.057
Is there a chance that
perhaps you gave the man

00:01:26.057 --> 00:01:27.691
an idea that maybe you wanted him to come

00:01:27.691 --> 00:01:29.162
look at the watch?

00:01:29.162 --> 00:01:30.873
- Maybe you're putting
off a vibe that said,

00:01:30.873 --> 00:01:32.522
"Hey, look at this watch."

00:01:32.522 --> 00:01:34.392
(saxophone music)

00:01:34.392 --> 00:01:35.636
The manner in which you were walking,

00:01:35.636 --> 00:01:37.992
would you say that you
were flashing the watch?

00:01:37.992 --> 00:01:38.983
- I wouldn't say that.

00:01:38.983 --> 00:01:40.692
- Maybe one could even say that you were

00:01:40.692 --> 00:01:41.525
advertising the watch.

00:01:41.525 --> 00:01:45.039
- Wait, can we just focus more
on the guy that mugged me?

00:01:45.039 --> 00:01:47.039
- Advertising the watch.

00:01:50.301 --> 00:01:52.503
- Listen, man, I wasn't
doing anything illegal.

00:01:52.503 --> 00:01:53.705
I was walking down the street.

00:01:53.705 --> 00:01:57.513
The guy that mugged me, that's illegal.

00:01:57.513 --> 00:02:00.285
- My sons are in sweatpants every day.

00:02:00.285 --> 00:02:03.118
(saxophone music)

